! ======================================================================
! test_v110_h2o_pbe_rt_field -- RT-TDDFT ladder step 2: a STATIC field
! switched on suddenly at t = 0 (the %efield operator and sign
! convention).  The post-switch Hamiltonian is time-independent, so
! the energy must be CONSERVED while the density genuinely oscillates.
!
! Water PBE/STO-3G, %rt_field 0.01 au along z, 100 steps of the
! default dt = 0.1 au.
!
! Reference (v1.10.0, 1 thread, reference BLAS):
!   Reference SCF energy (field-free): -75.227762250396
!   E(0) with the field term:          -75.221259897737
!     (E(0) = E_scf + 2 Tr[P0 V_rt]; the field-free part is
!      hard-checked against E_scf at startup)
!   Conservation summary over 100 steps:
!     max |E(t) - E(0)|   ~ 5e-11 Ha     <- THE monitor
!     max |N_e(t) - N_e|  ~ 1e-13 e
!     max idempotency     ~ 3e-14
!     max |mu(t) - mu(0)| ~ 3.6e-2 au    <- genuine dynamics
!   The predictor-corrector converges in <= 3 iterations/step at this
!   dt; at dt = 0.2 the same perturbation needs ~3-4 (the cap warning
!   then advises %rt_pc_maxiter 4).
! ======================================================================
%method  PBE
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%rt_tddft 100
%rt_dt    0.1
%rt_field 0.0 0.0 0.01
%rt_print_every 20
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
